<Metadata id="PilotStudyOutcomeOut"><Record name="PilotStudyOutcome" type="delimited"><Field name="study_visit_id" type="string"/><Field name="study_outcome" type="string"/><Field name="confirmed_nights" type="long"/><Field name="adjusted_nightly_rate" type="decimal"/><Field name="research_stay_value" type="decimal"/><Field name="review_note" type="string"/></Record></Metadata>

Business logic:
- Missing RoomPrototype produces DECLINED, zero numeric values, and ROOM_CONCEPT_UNKNOWN. A prototype_stage other than APPROVED also produces DECLINED, zero numeric values, and PROTOTYPE_NOT_APPROVED.
- Usable research capacity is research_nights minus blocked_nights, floored at zero; missing NightCapacity is zero. confirmed_nights is the lower of planned_nights and usable research capacity. study_outcome is CONFIRMED, PARTIALLY_CONFIRMED, or WAITLISTED accordingly.
- Apply a research incentive only when its row exists, rebate_percent is non-null, and either arrival_day falls in its inclusive campaign date range or both trial_track is LONG_STAY and planned_nights is at least qualifying_nights. Otherwise the rebate is zero.
- adjusted_nightly_rate is nightly_rate_lcy reduced by the rebate percent, but never below nightly_rate_lcy multiplied by minimum_rate_percent divided by 100. Round adjusted_nightly_rate and research_stay_value, where research_stay_value uses confirmed_nights. Rates are in the Eastern European hotel property's local currency, such as RON or BGN. review_note is NO_RESEARCH_CAPACITY for WAITLISTED, LIMITED_PILOT_CAPACITY for PARTIALLY_CONFIRMED, and null for CONFIRMED.

